# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# fetch-docs.mjs' own local cache -- always rebuilt from a real,
# checksummed release, never committed
/.docs-cache

# build-search-index.mjs' own output -- regenerated every build from
# .docs-cache, never committed
/public/search-index.json

# build-sidebar-index.mjs' own output -- same real convention
/public/sidebar/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are committed here, not ignored, and the
# arrangement matters.
#
# They ARE generated, by `next dev` (not `next build`, which is what the
# old ignore comment claimed and what misled a first attempt at this).
# next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js writes both, and its rule
# is: if AGENTS.md exists and carries the managed block, CLAUDE.md is
# skipped entirely. If AGENTS.md is absent, the block gets appended to
# the bottom of CLAUDE.md instead.
#
# So AGENTS.md is committed holding the managed block, which is what
# keeps a hand-written CLAUDE.md untouched and the tree clean on every
# `next dev`. That is exactly how ubx-docs-providers is arranged.
# Ignoring both meant neither existed, so `next dev` would scaffold
# AGENTS.md plus a CLAUDE.md containing only "@AGENTS.md".
